      "writtenOn": "2023-05-08T21:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should we error out if you specify both .aidl files and aidl_library deps?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 675,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 675,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "75524bcd967053dd5f93c551109c05356b482a80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43115d62_3ec68e97",
        "filename": "cc/compiler.go",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 675,
      "author": {
        "id": 1938760
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-11T17:59:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we shouldn\u0027t because it requires creating more modules than it should. `aidl_library` is provided to support strip import prefix and including aidl headers. Those aidl files without strip import prefix or aidl headers can be passed in via `srcs` prop.\n\nLet me know if you have any objection here.",
      "parentUuid": "ae20adb0_e0f54121",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 675,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 675,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "75524bcd967053dd5f93c551109c05356b482a80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23065ebc_a4a399ad",
        "filename": "cc/compiler.go",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 675,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-15T15:44:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`aidl_library` + cc rule will be how it looks in Bazel, so I don\u0027t think it\u0027s an issue to introduce that in Soong as well, but I don\u0027t feel strongly about this.\n\nInstead perhaps the error should be if `aidl_library` and `aidl.include_dirs` are set as they serve similar purposes but the former enables sandboxing while the latter prevents it.\n\nLooking at the logic below for handling aidl library vs .aidl files. Without disallowing `aidl.include_dirs` with `aidl_library`, there could be aidl include dirs that would be incompatible with `aidl_library` srcs being sandboxed.",
      "parentUuid": "43115d62_3ec68e97",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 675,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 675,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "75524bcd967053dd5f93c551109c05356b482a80",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
